<title>ESTONIA: TALLINN BOURSE REVIEWING OTC REQUIREMENTS.</title>
<headline>TALLINN BOURSE REVIEWING OTC REQUIREMENTS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Estonian stock exchange will consider how much information free market companies need to provide during a board meeting on Thursday.</p>
<p>The board meeting will be held at 1300GMT and a decision expected after 1500GMT, a stock exchange official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Official have already said that board will consider including an information provision requirement for the free market as none exists at the moment.</p>
<p>The free market companies are quoted on an over-the-counter basis and have less strict listing requirements than the official list.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +3 72 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
